NOTES: Build the surface as a single indexed BufferGeometry over the (x,y) grid with per-vertex color from a height ramp (blue → pink → violet), MeshLambert/MeshStandard with flatShading off, side = DoubleSide so the pit interior reads correctly. Clamp z to ±1.5 per vertex, which automatically yields the flat truncation caps; optionally add explicit circular disks at the clip planes so the caps are opaque. Contours: compute marching-squares polylines on the same scalar grid per frame and render as LineSegments offset ~0.005 along the surface normal (or use polygonOffset) to avoid z-fighting. For the top-down contour mode, tween the camera to elevation 90° and tween all z-values toward 0 rather than swapping objects, so the learner sees the relief flatten into the loops. Regenerate vertex positions/colors in place when either slider changes — do not rebuild geometry. Box is a LineSegments wireframe, no ticks or labels. Soft directional key light from upper-left plus ambient so the violet flanks stay readable; no shadows.

